# BookMeThat — Social Media Configuration

## Purpose
Configuration for the social media posting automation (Facebook, Instagram,
LinkedIn, X). Place your API tokens here — never commit real tokens.

## Free Tiers Only
- Instagram: Official Meta Graph API — free, no paid plans
- Facebook: Official Meta Graph API — free
- LinkedIn: Free tier available (no paid plan required)
- X: Official X API — free tier available

## Quick Start
1. Create the file: `cp social-media-config.yaml.example social-media-config.yaml`
2. Fill in your tokens (see setup skills below)
3. Run: `python scripts/social-media-posting.py --generate`
4. Review and publish: `python scripts/social-media-posting.py --publish`

## Token Setup

### Instagram / Facebook (Meta Graph API)
- Skill: `skills/instagram-automation` (README.md)
- Skill: `skills/facebook-api-setup` (SKILL.md)
- Required: `IG_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `IG_USER_ID`, `PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN`
- Save to: `~/.hermes/social-media-config.yaml` → `tokens:`

### LinkedIn (Official API or Apollo)
- Skill: `skills/linkedin-automation` (SKILL.md)
- Required: `LINKEDIN_TOKEN` (Shopify / OAuth token)
- Free tier only — no paid plan required

### X (Twitter) — Official API
- Skill: `skills/xurl` (SKILL.md)
- Required: `X_ACCESS_TOKEN` (from ~/.xurl)
- Setup: `xurl auth oauth2 --app my-app`

## Config Structure
```yaml
tokens:
  IG_ACCESS_TOKEN: "your_instagram_token"
  IG_USER_ID: "your_instagram_user_id"
  PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN: "your_facebook_page_token"
  LINKEDIN_TOKEN: "your_linkedin_token"
  X_ACCESS_TOKEN: "your_x_token"

platforms:
  - instagram
  - facebook
  - linkedin
  - x
```

## Important
- Never commit tokens to git
- Rotate tokens every ~55 days (before 60-day expiry)
- Store in `~/.hermes/social-media-config.yaml`
